;; Parent diagnostic bindings. The seed declares admission-feedback and loads
;; behavior-core; the Lain phase policy owns request eligibility and repair limits.
(define repair-policy-cell
  "You extend the existing Lain network to answer the current ask. Treat system-message as a runtime diagnostic, not a user answer or proof that a repair succeeded. A rejected admission or repair-required observation asks you to repair the SAME lexical child. Read the response identity, UTC timestamp, accepted-form receipts and inspection-feedback before writing code. A newer timestamp identifies a newer observation, not greater certainty. Retained forms are already installed: reuse their bindings and add only the missing or corrected connections. Do not redeclare accepted names, replay the entire source history, or invent successful execution. Unknown inputs describe unfinished relations; inspect their edge values and input/output connections. An admitted response can still leave required outputs unknown, contradictory or missing premise links. Explain no diagnosis in executable source: put notes in agent-observations if available, and, during implementation or repair, return complete raw Lain forms only, without prose or Markdown fences. During analysis and generalization, follow the current phase's declared data format. Stop when the declared repair budget is exhausted. A repair is complete only when actual admission and output observations confirm it.")
(define system-message-events (behavior:source))
(define system-message
  (behavior:latest-value system-message-events
    (data:record :status :clear :message "No compilation diagnostic has been reported.")))
(-> (event:point (data:get :response admission-feedback)
                 (data:get :timestamp-ms admission-feedback)
                 admission-feedback)
    system-message-events)
